From: SF2000 Linux project
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: hc15: do not consume DMA command completion twice

The DMA path waits for command completion before waiting for the DMA engine.
Do not enter the common PIO command-wait block afterward: the first wait has
already acknowledged the command IRQ, and a second wait can only time out once
the controller exposes its persistent command-control state accurately.

---
 drivers/mmc/host/hc15_mmc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/hc15_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/hc15_mmc.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/hc15_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/hc15_mmc.c
@@ -833,7 +833,8 @@ static void hc15_run_command(struct hc15_mmc *host, struct mmc_command *cmd,
 	else if (data && (data->flags & MMC_DATA_WRITE))
 		hc15_pio_write(host, data);
 
-	if (!data_write || !write_wait_first) {
+	/* DMA completion was already consumed before hc15_wait_dma(). */
+	if (!dma_xfer && (!data_write || !write_wait_first)) {
 		hc15_wait_irq(host, cmd, data != NULL);
 		hc15_get_response(host, cmd);
 	}
-- 
